Ṛgvedakhila(ºkāṇḍa,_ºsūkta)
additional hymns found spread over the different books of the Ṛv.; called also Ṛv. Pariśiṣṭa; Vālakhilya etc. belonging to this group are really very old, although Khilas are not included in Pada texts an. are found only in some mss. of Ṛv.; some of them are in Av. saṁhitā, some are q. in Nirukta itself. The Ṛgvidhāna notes 25 Khilas an. the Bṛhaddevatā refers to 37. Their number varies an. also variants are to be seen in mss. Max Mu7ller's edn. has a. end 32 Khilas according to the ms. used by him. (See IInd edn. Vol. IV, London, 1892). Aufrecht's edn. has 25; Indian edns. from 25 to 36, the last number [Page019-a. seen in Satavalekar's Aundh edn. (1940).
